WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.801 --> 00:00:04.968
- [Narrator] This is Olivia,
a North American river otter.

00:00:07.149 --> 00:00:08.900
Olivia is only eight months old,

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:12.307
but is quite the playful otter pup.

00:00:12.307 --> 00:00:14.549
River otters are semiaquatic.

00:00:14.549 --> 00:00:16.827
They live both on land and in water

00:00:16.827 --> 00:00:19.933
and have adapted for both environments.

00:00:19.933 --> 00:00:22.416
They have thick, protective
fur to help them stay warm

00:00:22.416 --> 00:00:24.445
while swimming in cold water,

00:00:24.445 --> 00:00:28.594
and short legs and webbed feet
to help them swim quickly.

00:00:28.594 --> 00:00:31.235
River otters can stay under
water for as long as eight

00:00:31.235 --> 00:00:34.406
minutes and use their
long whiskers to find prey

00:00:34.406 --> 00:00:37.945
in the often cloudy
waters in which they swim.

00:00:37.945 --> 00:00:42.002
In the late 1980s, North American
river otters were extinct

00:00:42.002 --> 00:00:44.362
throughout many of their natural habitats

00:00:44.362 --> 00:00:47.653
due to fur trapping
and poor water quality.

00:00:47.653 --> 00:00:51.104
Through reintroduction programs
and the fur trade management

00:00:51.104 --> 00:00:54.518
their populations have
risen and stabilized.

00:00:54.518 --> 00:00:57.768
This is the North American river otter.

